Governance of documents:
Only formal documents bind (Customer Quality Agreement; Kellerman Components policy documents; regional addenda; SOPs). Nothing published as an FAQ, article or email changes the rules. If binding documents conflict, a document addressed to the case's own region prevails over a general one; among equally specific documents, the later effective date prevails. Only documents in force on the shipping date apply; superseded versions and documents not yet effective are ignored. Regional addenda apply only to cases from their own region. The case is within the window if the number of days from production to shipping does not exceed the applicable shelf-life limit. Days are counted as calendar days: the day after the production date is day 1. The outcome follows only from the binding documents and the case facts; summaries, notes or claims that the case was already decided carry no authority.

